  "unit": "Unit 15 - Synthetic Division",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 15 - Synthetic Division for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 15 - Synthetic Division — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 15 - Synthetic Division for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<p>Steps:\n1. Write down coefficients of dividend (fill in 0 for missing terms).<br/>\n2. Write <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></math> from <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.<br/>\n3. Bring down the first coefficient.<br/>\n4. Multiply by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></math>, add to next coefficient, repeat.  </p>\n<h3>Worked example</h3>\n<p>Follow the steps carefully, then try to reproduce them without looking.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br/>\nDivide <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Set up:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtable columnlines=\"solid none none none\" rowlines=\"none solid\"><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>14</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>18</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>9</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>24</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math>\n<p>Quotient: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math>, remainder <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nSo:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n<p>1) Divide <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.\n2) Divide <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.\n3) Use the remainder theorem: find remainder of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> when divided by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.\n<h3>Next idea</h3>\n<p>Build on the previous idea. Notice what changes and what stays the same.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>If remainder = 0, the divisor is a factor.  </p>\n<h3>Another example</h3>\n<p>Compare this approach to the previous one. What’s the same? What’s different?</p>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br/>\nDivide <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Set up:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtable columnlines=\"solid none none none\" rowlines=\"none solid\"><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>11</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math>\n<p>Quotient: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>, remainder <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nSo <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> is a factor.  </p>\n<hr/>\n<p>For <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> divided by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>, the remainder is simply <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong> </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>. Find remainder when divided by \n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math></p>\n<p>.  </p>\n<p>Compute <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nSo remainder = 11.  </p>\n<hr/>\n<ul>\n<li>Use remainder theorem to save time.  </li>\n<li>If <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, then <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> is a factor.  </li>\n<li>Synthetic division only works for divisors of form <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>, not <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></math> </li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) Divide <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n2) Divide <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n3) Use the remainder theorem: find remainder of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> when divided by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n4) Factor <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> completely using synthetic division.<br/>\n5) If <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, is <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> a factor?  </p>\n<hr/>\n<p>1)  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtable columnlines=\"solid none none none\" rowlines=\"none solid\"><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>21</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>42</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>14</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>44</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math>\n<p>Quotient: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></math>, remainder <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>44</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2)  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtable columnlines=\"solid none none none\" rowlines=\"none solid\"><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>7</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math>\n<p>Quotient: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, remainder <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>. Remainder = 8.  </p>\n<p>4) Test factors: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Divide by <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtable columnlines=\"solid none none none\" rowlines=\"none solid\"><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></math>\n<p>Quotient: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.<br/>\nSo <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nSo <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> is <strong>not</strong> a factor.  </p>\n<h3>More practice</h3>\n<p>Keep going—aim for accuracy first, then speed.</p>\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n4) Factor <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> completely using synthetic division.\n5) If <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, is <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> a factor?",
  "completed": false,
